## Owner Creation Code Map

### 1. REST controller method (POST create owner)

**File:** `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain7/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

The `addOwner` method (lines 99-109) handles `POST /api/owners`. It maps the incoming `OwnerFieldsDto` to an `Owner`, saves it via the service, and returns `201 CREATED`:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

The actual `@RequestMapping`/`POST` path binding comes from the generated `OwnersApi` interface (`target/generated-sources/openapi/.../rest/api/OwnersApi.java`) that this controller implements. Note there is also a **V2 controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) but it only exposes a paged list endpoint (`listOwnersPage`); it does NOT create owners.

### 2. Owner entity — `city` field

**File:** `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain7/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`Owner` extends `Person`. The `city` field is at lines 43-45 with getter/setter at 76-82:

```java
@Column(name = "city")
@NotEmpty
private String city;
...
public String getCity() { return this.city; }
public void setCity(String city) { this.city = city; }
```

Other notable fields: `address`, `telephone` (digits-only normalized in setter), `email`, `registrationDate`, `membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, and `pets`.

### 3. Service layer (saves owners)

**Interface:** `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain7/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java`

**Impl:** `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain7/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

`saveOwner` (lines 237-255) contains the create-time business logic — it sets registration date, membership number, generates a customer code, and checks for duplicate telephone/email:

```java
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
        }
        owner.setMembershipNumber(ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1);
        owner.setCustomerCode(generateCustomerCode(owner));
        if (isDuplicateTelephone(owner)) { throw new DuplicateOwnerException(...); }
        if (isDuplicateEmail(owner)) { throw new DuplicateOwnerException(...); }
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

**City is used here** in `generateCustomerCode` (lines 263-271) — it builds a code `<UPPERCASE_CITY>-<NNNN>` by counting existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive), by streaming `ownerRepository.findAll()`:

```java
